On Thu, 1 Jul 1999, Xu Fan wrote:

> 
> While using nnet function for prediction, I got different answers when
> running the same codes for the second time. Any reason and/or remedy?

Yes. You need to read the documentation more carefully. nnet is not a 
determinstic algorithm, and is designed to search out multiple local
minima. Indeed, it is run repeatedly for this purpose on V&R2 pp. 490-2.

-- 
