On Thu, 1 Jul 1999, Prof Brian D Ripley wrote:

>Well of course I know that. My bet is that no user of S-PLUS has ever used
>more than 10% of the period in a real simulation.

I have done simulations which have pushed if not exceeded the limits of the
RNG's period.  I also know other people who have done the same.  I have at
times run bootstrap-calibration code in S-PLUS.  To do this, I resampled
the (generated) data 1,000,000 times.  My samples sizes were as large as
10,000.  Therefore, I had to randomly pick 10^10 observations from the
(generated) data and hope that they were I.I.D.  Of course, I don't make a
practice of doing such things in S-PLUS, but sometimes it is far quicker in
(human) time to setup something in S-PLUS and let it run for a week than
code it in C.

I've long worried about the properties of S-PLUS's (MatLabs's and GAUSS's)
random number generators.  Given this discussion, I will make certain to
exclusively use generators (written in Fortran or C) whose properties I
know and like!

Cheers,
Jas.

