From: jsekhon at fas.harvard.edu
Date: Thu, 01 Jul 1999 15:03:55 -0400
Subject: Re: [S] Does the new version of S-Plus fix num acc. and RNG problems?
In-Reply-To: <Pine.WNT.4.05.9907011916450.16901-100000@tern.stats>
References: <9907011754.AA21058@haberman.ne.mediaone.net> <Pine.WNT.4.05.9907011916450.16901-100000@tern.stats>
Message-ID: <9907011903.AA21054@haberman.ne.mediaone.net>

>You have not come anywhere near the period, which is ca 4.6 x 10^18. Quite
>a large number!  I gave some timings that might have made you realize
>that.

I need 1,000,000 draws to estimate the model ONCE.  I have 10,000 Monte
Carlo simulations and 100 experimental conditions.  I also need to generate
the data for each Monte Carlo simulation and that requires the creation of
obs*variables (10,000*5) double numbers.  Now that's getting to be a LARGE
number of draws: about 5*10^16.  This isn't more than the period you
report, but getting "close".  And this doesn't even touch upon the issue of
serial correlation which would entirely invalidate the experiment.

Moreover, doing 1,000,000 redraws for a bootstrap calibration is
conservative.  If I added another calibration loop, that would bring the
number of draws to about 5*10^19.

Jas.

