And how do they prove that they are `truly random'?  Most attempts to build
physical random generators have been

(i) too slow for leading-dege applications
(ii) not sufficiently uncorrelated.

The physical mechanism may be random and independent, but the recording
mechanism usually is not.

I am signing off this topic now: discuss amongst yourselves after reading
the literature.

