From feldesmanm at pdx.edu  Wed Jul  7 18:58:56 1999
From: feldesmanm at pdx.edu (Marc R. Feldesman)
Date: Wed, 07 Jul 1999 11:58:56 -0700
Subject: [S] Re: How to get rid of opening Report Window
Message-ID: <4.2.0.58.19990707115433.009f4ab0@pop4.ibm.net>

Thanks to Stephen Weller of Mathsoft for quickly providing me a solution to 
the annoying opening Report problem.

The relevant part of Stephen's message is below:

============================================

It is possible to change your default S-PLUS Text Output Routing to
echo startup warnings/messages to a Commands Windows instead. You
could modify your .First() function to look as follows:

> .First <- function()
{
     setTextOutputRouting(normalTextWindow = "Commands",
                          errorWindow="Default")
     library(Mass)
     library(Hmisc)

You may like this behavior better.

You can also change Text Output Routing via the "Options |
Text Output Routing" menu, but your changes will only stick for the
current Splus session.
=================================================

The first solution - new line 1 of the .First() function - solves the 
problem easily and makes SP2000 behave like SP4.5R2.

The second solution doesn't work at all because the Report Window came up 
the minute that the .First file was executed.  It wouldn't be possible to 
let that stick in a session in which the event I wanted to stop had already 
occurred before I had the opportunity to change the within-session behavior.

