From timh at statsci.com  Wed Jul  7 20:22:28 1999
From: timh at statsci.com (Tim Hesterberg)
Date: Wed, 07 Jul 1999 13:22:28 -0700
Subject: Re: [S] Re: bivariate Gaussian dist.
In-Reply-To: <E111qXM-0000sj-00@harris.cc.strath.ac.uk>
Message-ID: <199907072022.NAA23960@quake.statsci.com>

Usman G. Shehu" <usman at stams.strath.ac.uk> wrote:

>I would like to generate random sample from bivariate Gaussian
>distribution with unity covariance matrix. How could I do that?

and followed up:

>Thank you to all those who responded to my question. 
>The easiest way is to use the "rmultnorm" function, which is available
>in UNIX version.

The rmultnorm function is defined in the help file for rnorm under S-PLUS 3.4.

In S-PLUS 4.0 and higher, there is a new function "rmvnorm".
This allows greater flexibility in specifying the joint distribution.
In this case you could do any of:
        rmvnorm(n, d=2)
        rmvnorm(n, rho=0)
        rmvnorm(n, cov=diag(2))

For the special case of an identity covariance matrix you can also do:
        matrix(rnorm(2*n), ncol=2)

