From B.Rowlingson at lancaster.ac.uk  Fri Jul  9 15:13:36 1999
From: B.Rowlingson at lancaster.ac.uk (Baz)
Date: Fri, 09 Jul 1999 16:13:36 +0100
Subject: [S] Splus 5.1 help enhancement
Message-ID: <378611A0.966FDA10@lancs.ac.uk>

 Just installed Splus5.1 for Solaris today. Nice to have
help.start() back, even if it is now a slow Java/Javascript
thing. The help system also relies on you running Netscape
on the same machine as Splus, since it uses local file URL's
for Netscape to find the docs. I normally run Netscape on my
linux workstation and Splus on the Solaris box, so I have to
run another Netscape on the Solaris box to read help... Never
mind, we're moving to Linux soon so no problem in the future.

 I digress. Enhancement time. When the help.start() system
pops up a help page, its one of those slimline Netscape
browser windows with no menu or button bar. Takes up less
screen, but I couldn't find a way of printing the help text.

Solution: edit the file:

 $SHOME/splus/lib/X11/helpstart/all.html

 at the top, you'll see the definition for the win_help function
- change one line to this:

open(url,"srch_trm","width=600,height=500,resizable=1,
scrolling=1,statusbar=1,location=1,scrollbars=1,menubar=1");

 ie add 'menubar=1'. This will give you a Netscape menu bar, 
from which you can print, save, view source etc. You can even
add Splus help pages to your bookmarks...

 Hope thats useful....

Barry Rowlingson
Computing Officer
Dept of Maths and Stats
Lancaster University
UK
