On Fri, 16 Jul 1999, BILL COX wrote:

> Does anyone aware of any routines for computing
> Expectation Maximization (EM).

This is an FAQ (literally). EM is not an algorithm nor something that can
be computed: it is a method for devising algorithms.

In some circles it is a misnomer for fitting mixtures of Gaussians: library
mda uses the EM algorithm to do so (by `maximum likelihood').

