From: Joseph S. Verducci <jsv at stat.ohio-state.edu>

Is 

       matrix(rank(a),nrow(a),ncol(a))

what you want?

Example:
> a
     [,1] [,2] [,3] 
[1,]   27   24   29
[2,]   21   22   28
[3,]   23   26   25

> sort(a)
[1] 21 22 23 24 25 26 27 28 29

> matrix(rank(a),nrow(a),ncol(a))
     [,1] [,2] [,3] 
[1,]    7    4    9
[2,]    1    2    8
[3,]    3    6    5

From: Jim Hughes <hughes at diamond.cfas.washington.edu>

Kim -

Does this do what you want?

ord <- order(mat)
mat[ord] # orders the elements of the matrix mat
cbind(row(mat)[ord],col(mat)[ord]) # gives the row, col index of each
                                   # ordered element in the original matrix
Jim

