The answer was simple:

On Wed, 28 Jul 1999,  Clark Sims  wrote:

> 
>  Going through the online help, I see that most
> of the GUI interface is directly analogous to
> commands from the command line. However when I
> do work in the GUI, nothing appears in the history box
> (when I press CTRL i). Is there a way to make the 
> corresponding text commands appear on the command line?
> Is there a way of editing and repeating GUI commands?

Chuck Taylor wrote:

Yes. There are two kinds of history windows, the one you are seeing which
excludes GUI commands, and another one that includes gui commands. Look under
the Window | History menu and you will see three entries:

        Display
        Clear
        Commands... Ctrl+I

The third menu option is for Commands Window history only, and the first two
are the ones that give you what you are asking for in the form of a script
window.

